# AeroShield dashboard configuration.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Only .env.local is gitignored (see ./.gitignore); this template is committed and
# must never contain a real key. Vite exposes variables prefixed VITE_ to the
# browser bundle — anything here is PUBLIC, so the only safe value is a key that is
# safe to publish.
#
# The ingest key (drone:ingest) belongs on the Jetson, never in a browser build.
# What belongs here is the DASHBOARD key: detections:read, which grants read access
# to detections plus the review/copilot/report actions the UI already performs
# on-screen. It is the least-privileged key that makes the wired API paths live.

# Leave unset (or empty) and every call in src/lib/api.ts keeps its fixture
# fallback — the zero-key classroom demo runs with this file absent entirely.
# Set it and the dashboard talks to the backend at http://127.0.0.1:8000
# (proxied through Vite in dev — see vite.config.ts).
#
#   cd backend && python scripts/create_api_key.py --name dashboard --preset dashboard
#
VITE_DASHBOARD_KEY=
